    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Assuming the parents are chosen independently, $ \\Pr(g_f, g_m) = \\Pr(g_f) \\cdot \\Pr(g_m) $. Further, if genotypes are in Hardy-Weinberg proportions, parental genotype frequencies are completely specified by the frequency $ p $ of allele $ Q $, e.g.,",
