    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ p(z) $ is the phenotypic density function for the entire population. Parental phenotypes are then incorporated by replacing $ \\Pr(g) $ by $ \\Pr(g \\mid z) $. Equation 13.12 follows directly from Bayes' theorem (Equation 13.24), which will be discussed shortly.",
